From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Playport <dev@playport.invalid>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 22:49:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: write an i386 child's debug output from its window on
 iOS

wow64_wine_dbg_write took the guest string's address as a host one, so
write() failed with EFAULT and every line an i386 child of the iOS
session printed was lost. Add the caller's window base (madeira-unix
0049) when it has one.

Class: diagnostics
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-03-portal2-wow64-pointers.md
Offered-upstream: no; the window exists only on the iOS port
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/debug.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/debug.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/debug.c
index 53516b9..ac4c2b7 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/debug.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/debug.c
@@ -289,7 +289,13 @@ NTSTATUS wow64_wine_dbg_write( void *args )
         ULONG        str;
         unsigned int len;
     } const *params32 = args;
+#ifdef WINE_IOS
+    /* an i386 child's string is in its window, not at the guest address */
+    extern uintptr_t ios_wow64_current_base(void);
+    uintptr_t base = ios_wow64_current_base();
 
+    if (base && params32->str) return write( 2, (char *)base + params32->str, params32->len );
+#endif
     return write( 2, ULongToPtr(params32->str), params32->len );
 }
 #endif
